# Future Digital Plus UI Kit: the repository root is the package root (package.json is here).
#
# Rules for this file:
#   - never ignore *.meta (GUIDs must be committed, Unity needs them in every consumer)
#   - never ignore a '<name>~' folder (Samples~, Documentation~, Tools~ are part of the package) and so never add a catch-all '*~'
#   - never ignore *.dll or *.pdb (the four UIComponents Roslyn DLLs and the NSubstitute test DLLs are needed)
#   - never ignore *.csproj below Tools~ (CompileCheck, LintRunner and PureTests are dotnet projects of the kit)

# macOS, editors
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/
*.swp
*.swo

# Unity output: only appears when the repository root is opened as a Unity project (normally it is referenced by a game or a scratch project)
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/[Rr]ecordings/
/*.csproj
/*.sln
/*.slnx
/*.suo
/*.user
/*.pidb
/*.booproj
/*.unityproj
sysinfo.txt
crashlytics-build.properties

# Build and test output of the Tools~ projects and scripts
bin/
obj/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
TestResults/
*.trx

# Secrets and local configuration: never commit
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
*.secret

# FutureDigitalPlus: the same re-includes the package always carried. This file is also copied into a classic Assets copy of the kit
# (Tools~/make_classic_kit.py), and a game repository's own .gitignore often has a catch-all '*~' (backup files) and '*.dll', which would silently
# drop Documentation~/, Samples~/, Tools~/ and the Roslyn DLLs. These two lines win over such a pattern in the game repository.
!*~/
!*.dll
